{"type":"route","meta":{"status":200,"headers":{"cache-control":"public, max-age=3600","content-type":"application/rss+xml; charset=utf-8","x-next-cache-tags":"_N_T_/layout,_N_T_/(marketing)/layout,_N_T_/(marketing)/blog/layout,_N_T_/(marketing)/blog/rss.xml/layout,_N_T_/(marketing)/blog/rss.xml/route,_N_T_/blog/rss.xml"}},"body":"<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n<rss version=\"2.0\" xmlns:atom=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\" xmlns:dc=\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\">\n  <channel>\n    <title>Amantrika Blog</title>\n    <link>http://localhost:3000/blog</link>\n    <description>Guides, traditions and planning notes for Indian weddings and digital invitations.</description>\n    <language>en-in</language>\n    <atom:link href=\"http://localhost:3000/blog/rss.xml\" rel=\"self\" type=\"application/rss+xml\" />\n    <lastBuildDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 03:30:00 GMT</lastBuildDate>\n    <item>\n      <title>Sharing your wedding invitation on WhatsApp without it getting lost</title>\n      <link>http://localhost:3000/blog/sharing-your-wedding-invitation-on-whatsapp</link>\n      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">http://localhost:3000/blog/sharing-your-wedding-invitation-on-whatsapp</guid>\n      <description>What to write around the link, when to send it, and why a bare forwarded URL gets ignored by exactly the guests you most want to reach.</description>\n      <category>Guides</category>\n      <dc:creator>The Amantrika Team</dc:creator>\n      <pubDate>Sun, 02 Aug 2026 03:30:00 GMT</pubDate>\n    </item>\n    <item>\n      <title>Choosing a wedding invitation theme that still looks right in six months</title>\n      <link>http://localhost:3000/blog/choosing-a-wedding-invitation-theme</link>\n      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">http://localhost:3000/blog/choosing-a-wedding-invitation-theme</guid>\n      <description>How to pick a visual style for your invitation: what to match it to, what to ignore, and the tests worth running before you commit.</description>\n      <category>Inspiration</category>\n      <dc:creator>Prachi Jain</dc:creator>\n      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 03:30:00 GMT</pubDate>\n    </item>\n    <item>\n      <title>How to collect wedding RSVPs without three hundred WhatsApp replies</title>\n      <link>http://localhost:3000/blog/collect-wedding-rsvps-without-whatsapp-chaos</link>\n      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">http://localhost:3000/blog/collect-wedding-rsvps-without-whatsapp-chaos</guid>\n      <description>Why Indian weddings are hard to count, what to ask for instead of a yes or no, and how to get a headcount the caterer can actually work from.</description>\n      <category>Planning</category>\n      <dc:creator>The Amantrika Team</dc:creator>\n      <pubDate>Sat, 04 Jul 2026 03:30:00 GMT</pubDate>\n    </item>\n    <item>\n      <title>The ceremonies in a Hindu wedding, and which ones your invitation should name</title>\n      <link>http://localhost:3000/blog/hindu-wedding-ceremonies-explained</link>\n      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">http://localhost:3000/blog/hindu-wedding-ceremonies-explained</guid>\n      <description>From roka to vidaai: what each ceremony is, roughly when it happens, and how to put the schedule on an invitation so guests know where to be.</description>\n      <category>Traditions</category>\n      <dc:creator>The Amantrika Team</dc:creator>\n      <pubDate>Thu, 11 Jun 2026 03:30:00 GMT</pubDate>\n    </item>\n    <item>\n      <title>Digital or printed wedding invitations: an honest comparison</title>\n      <link>http://localhost:3000/blog/digital-vs-printed-wedding-invitations</link>\n      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">http://localhost:3000/blog/digital-vs-printed-wedding-invitations</guid>\n      <description>What each format actually does well, what it costs, and why most Indian families end up using both — with a rule for deciding who gets which.</description>\n      <category>Planning</category>\n      <dc:creator>The Amantrika Team</dc:creator>\n      <pubDate>Sat, 09 May 2026 03:30:00 GMT</pubDate>\n    </item>\n    <item>\n      <title>How to word an Indian wedding invitation, in English and Hindi</title>\n      <link>http://localhost:3000/blog/how-to-word-a-wedding-invitation</link>\n      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">http://localhost:3000/blog/how-to-word-a-wedding-invitation</guid>\n      <description>Who invites whom, where the parents&apos; names go, and ready-to-use wording for the wedding, sangeet, mehndi and reception in both languages.</description>\n      <category>Guides</category>\n      <dc:creator>Prachi Jain</dc:creator>\n      <pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 03:30:00 GMT</pubDate>\n    </item>\n    <item>\n      <title>How to create a wedding invitation website in about fifteen minutes</title>\n      <link>http://localhost:3000/blog/step-by-step-guide-to-create-wedding-website</link>\n      <guid isPermaLink=\"true\">http://localhost:3000/blog/step-by-step-guide-to-create-wedding-website</guid>\n      <description>A practical walkthrough for building a digital wedding invitation, from gathering details to sharing the link with three hundred relatives.</description>\n      <category>Guides</category>\n      <dc:creator>Prachi Jain</dc:creator>\n      <pubDate>Sat, 14 Mar 2026 03:30:00 GMT</pubDate>\n    </item>\n  </channel>\n</rss>"}